      "writtenOn": "2024-07-30T07:36:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Is it possible to unwind this loop to the upper layer call? What I mean is that `CpPresetOperationCaller()` has the context of all the devices and iterates over all of them by calling `CpPresetIndexOperationWriteReq()` with a narrowed down context for each device, and here you again expand the context to iterating over all the devices for each single device call. As a result we do all these operations here N^2 times, while we could do it just N times on the higher level loop.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 497,
        "startChar": 6,
        "endLine": 497,
        "endChar": 36
      },
      "revId": "4b1c8c88c3c1460f8fb6373db6657286c52bba30",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b65ddfff_fac12cf9",
        "filename": "system/bta/has/has_client.cc",
        "patchSetId": 8
      },
      "lineNbr": 497,
      "author": {
        "id": 3446464
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-07-31T08:52:01Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I noticed it, but checking it earlier will break unit tests: there are checks for device capabilities (like `IsConnected`, `SupportsPresets` etc.). And we should check the flag as the last thing. So if we want to move this check higher, rest will need to follow, but I\u0027m not sure if this is correct approach? I see these kind of checks only in corresponding `WriteReq` methods, not in `CpPresetOperationCaller`",
      "parentUuid": "366e755e_affe413c",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 497,
        "startChar": 6,
        "endLine": 497,
        "endChar": 36
      },
      "revId": "4b1c8c88c3c1460f8fb6373db6657286c52bba30",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
